05"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T07:22:26-08:00","id":790850,"title":"","content":"That's easy: Lhiannon use banes and fuck up the spiritual landscape. They're already up there on the Garou's shit list, according to Werewolf: the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:04:21-08:00","id":791111,"title":"","content":"The use of Thirst of Donn probably has the following effects in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> Plant spirits in the affected area like Glade Children and the like either go into slumber, or lose Essence. <br /> <br /> Animal spirits feel uneasy and do not think the place is clean, so they avoid it.<br /> <br /> Land spirits that represent the geographic area lose traits and Essence.<br /> <br /> Appropriate Banes are attracted to the area and begin preying on the weakened or isolated Gaian spirits.<br /> <br /> Enough draining might shift the Gauntlet rating up by one to reflect the death of the spiritual energies.<br /> <br /> If a Caern is nearby, the Caern Totem could feel alarm, worry, or sickness. It might even begin losing Gnosis en route to its rank declining (temporarily).<br /> <br /> The look of the Penumbra should show obvious signs of distress from what it was before. While certain ephemeral landmarks might be recognizable, the damage will be very apparent - the equivalent of various plant diseases wiping out forests or fields in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user